  "orientation_note": "Investigated, not assumed: the naive 'messier -> less compressible per byte' expectation is INVERTED on this generator. The knob injects textual redundancy (duplicated scaffolding, repeated boilerplate, marker comments) and longer files amortize the zlib header, so the raw compressed/original ratio FALLS monotonically with the knob (see level_means). The anchor is therefore oriented as redundancy = 1 - ratio, direction '+'. NCD needs no flip: distance from the clean reference rises with the knob.",
